    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d56-a1">

                <pb facs="0201" n="77" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg77"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    46.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Carrillo to Mr. Adams</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1880-11-13"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 13,
                    1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Repeating the acknowledgments of my
                    government for the benevolent offices and personal attitude of your excellency
                    during the peace negotiations, I have the honor to transmit three copies of a
                    pamphlet, in which these conferences have been published.</p>
                <p>I improve the opportunity to again subscribe myself, with all consideration and
                    respect, your excellency’s, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. C. CARRILLO.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>To his excellency the <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister Resident of the
                            United States of North America</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Present</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
